@startuml concurrency-model
' liblevenshtein — read/write concurrency model, grouped by how READS are coordinated.
' Every dictionary backend is Send + Sync and cheap to share via Arc; what differs is
' whether a reader can proceed without blocking a concurrent writer.
' Color legend:
'   concurrency  #CFD8DC (blue-grey)  = the two read-coordination groups
'   in-memory    #E8F5E9 (green)      = in-memory backends
'   disk         #E0F2F1 (teal)       = disk-persisted (durable) backends
'   border/arrow #455A64 (slate)
' Grouping is by actual read behaviour, not the (sometimes coarse) SyncStrategy enum —
' e.g. DoubleArrayTrie reports ExternalSync yet is immutable, so its reads never block.
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam rectangle {
  RoundCorner 14
  BorderColor #455A64
  FontColor #102027
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFF3E0
  BorderColor #EF6C00
}
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowThickness 2

title Concurrency model — dictionary reads grouped by synchronization strategy

rectangle "All dictionaries: Send + Sync · Arc cheap-clone" as banner #CFD8DC

rectangle "Lock-free / wait-free reads — readers never block a writer" as gfree #CFD8DC {
  rectangle "DoubleArrayTrie(Char)\nimmutable array · 𝒪(1) reads · static" as dat #E8F5E9
  rectangle "DynamicDawgU64\nper-node ArcSwap RCU · CAS writes" as ddu64 #E8F5E9
  rectangle "PathMapSnapshot / PathMapRef(Char)\npersistent copy-on-write snapshot" as pms #E8F5E9
  rectangle "PersistentARTrie(Char / U64)\nlock-free CAS overlay · mmap" as part #E0F2F1
  rectangle "PersistentScdawg / PersistentSuffixAutomaton /\nPersistentSuffixTree(Char)\nArcSwap graph · disk-persisted" as psub #E0F2F1
  rectangle "PersistentVocabARTrie\nlock-free overlay · term ↔ id · disk" as pv #E0F2F1
}

rectangle "RwLock readers (parking_lot · ExternalSync) — reads block only a concurrent writer" as glock #CFD8DC {
  rectangle "DynamicDawg(Char)\nArc<RwLock<DawgCore>> · SIMD + bloom" as dd #E8F5E9
  rectangle "SuffixAutomaton(Char)\nArc<RwLock<…>> · substring" as sa #E8F5E9
  rectangle "Scdawg(Char)\nArc<RwLock<…>> · bidirectional" as sc #E8F5E9
  rectangle "PathMapDictionary(Char)\nbrief RwLock → snapshot, then lock-free walk" as pmd #E8F5E9
  rectangle "BijectiveMap\ntwo RwLocks: forward DAWG + reverse HashMap" as bij #E8F5E9
}

note bottom of glock
  Intended direction: the in-memory RwLock-guarded dynamic backends
  (DynamicDawg · SuffixAutomaton · Scdawg) are slated to adopt the
  lock-free reader model already shipping on DynamicDawgU64 and the
  Persistent* family. PathMapDictionary only locks to grab an 𝒪(1)
  snapshot, then traverses lock-free.
end note

banner -[#455A64,thickness=3]down-> gfree
banner -[#455A64,thickness=3]down-> glock

@enduml
